{"id": "EUVD-2026-28711", "enisaUuid": "e614c7a3-1ed7-36d3-8918-d91acffefb3f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlibceph: Use u32 for non-negative values in ceph_monmap_decode()\n\nThis patch fixes unnecessary implicit conversions that change signedness\nof blob_len and num_mon in ceph_monmap_decode().\nCurrently blob_len and num_mon are (signed) int variables. They are used\nto hold values that are always non-negative and get assigned in\nceph_decode_32_safe(), which is meant to assign u32 values. Both\nvariables are subsequently used as unsigned values, and the value of\nnum_mon is further assigned to monmap->num_mon, which is of type u32.\nTherefore, both variables should be of type u32. This is especially\nrelevant for num_mon. If the value read from the incoming message is\nvery large, it is interpreted as a negative value, and the check for\nnum_mon > CEPH_MAX_MON does not catch it. This leads to the attempt to\nallocate a very large chunk of memory for monmap, which will most likely\nfail. In this case, an unnecessary attempt to allocate memory is\nperformed, and -ENOMEM is returned instead of -EINVAL.", "datePublished": "2026-05-08T14:21:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:16:28", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee5588e2bc41acb73f6676c0520420c107cd0140", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86f7060cd638d6eb042e8ed780fb83a59ca0dcb3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f2806684b05bd24d05c091083b8e2517ba8ffac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b268984ae88cb0dcd7a8e8263962c748448e26e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba0a4df8c563536857dcbf7b4dbd0f2a15f57ace", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08bc6173fd611ad5a40f472bf5f15b92aea0fe40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/770444611f047dbfd4517ec0bc1b179d40c2f346"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43405", "GHSA-5r63-pv2h-4jqg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.7, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1710b785-d05c-3cc9-a6d2-1eb6d7479029", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cbd5fc22d5043a8a76e15d75d031fe24d1f69c <08bc6173fd611ad5a40f472bf5f15b92aea0fe40"}, {"id": "25ba33af-89fa-3128-a0ad-c12e03e394ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.9"}, {"id": "295c5468-d909-35f0-8060-ce70c3766abe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cbd5fc22d5043a8a76e15d75d031fe24d1f69c <ee5588e2bc41acb73f6676c0520420c107cd0140"}, {"id": "2eddc312-bad9-3cdd-9a77-c8b7df2f8394", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.167"}, {"id": "4313a5a3-75aa-3c14-a700-2dc4cd1a7181", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.19"}, {"id": "4e3bf920-c69a-3706-8edb-e6f7d32975c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.203"}, {"id": "57d96220-891b-3d25-a8d6-50b45a18ea5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cbd5fc22d5043a8a76e15d75d031fe24d1f69c <86f7060cd638d6eb042e8ed780fb83a59ca0dcb3"}, {"id": "700f72aa-55e6-3408-8802-10c374256fc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.130"}, {"id": "7868eec7-0edb-397d-8dcd-949b83844a66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "80d23a9f-5db7-3701-a1f5-4e9eed44a8ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cbd5fc22d5043a8a76e15d75d031fe24d1f69c <770444611f047dbfd4517ec0bc1b179d40c2f346"}, {"id": "83820732-9842-39d9-b719-d3eadcbe3a69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cbd5fc22d5043a8a76e15d75d031fe24d1f69c <5f2806684b05bd24d05c091083b8e2517ba8ffac"}, {"id": "a48938c0-8ec7-362c-9801-612930ac696f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cbd5fc22d5043a8a76e15d75d031fe24d1f69c <b268984ae88cb0dcd7a8e8263962c748448e26e8"}, {"id": "a9bd6722-86fa-31fc-a267-bae62248b0df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b5ab0ef8-50f6-3881-99aa-c027aed74e4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11"}, {"id": "d3e50e51-8336-3dfb-8fb8-268df21074c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cbd5fc22d5043a8a76e15d75d031fe24d1f69c <ba0a4df8c563536857dcbf7b4dbd0f2a15f57ace"}, {"id": "f55268cb-4ca8-31bb-950b-547e57c18547", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.78"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b87be6c8-9c0d-3dc3-9a19-42e6312fbab7", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}